<li id="bib.bib28" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_bibitem">[28]</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Hoang Anh Dau, Anthony Bagnall, Kaveh Kamgar, Chin-Chia Michael Yeh, Yan Zhu,
Shaghayegh Gharghabi, Chotirat Ann Ratanamahatana, and Eamonn Keogh,

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">“The ucr time series archive,”

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">IEEE/CAA Journal of Automatica Sinica</span>, vol. 6, no. 6, pp.
1293–1305, November 2019.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib29" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_bibitem">[29]</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Alejandro Parada-Mayorga, Leopoldo Agorio, Alejandro Ribeiro, and Juan
Bazerque,

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">“Convolutional filtering with rkhs algebras,”

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span id="bib.bib29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing</span>, 2025.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem 1.</span> Define the scaled Lagrange basis on <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\cup\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\cup\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L_{\alpha}(t)\;=\;\frac{t}{\alpha}\prod_{\beta\in\Lambda,\,\beta\neq\alpha}\cdot\frac{t-\beta}{\alpha-\beta},\qquad t\in\mathbb{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\alpha}(t)\;=\;\frac{t}{\alpha}\prod_{\beta\in\Lambda,\,\beta\neq\alpha}\cdot\frac{t-\beta}{\alpha-\beta},\qquad t\in\mathbb{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\alpha}(\alpha)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\alpha}(\alpha)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\alpha}(\beta)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\alpha}(\beta)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\alpha}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\alpha}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\Lambda\setminus\{\alpha\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\Lambda\setminus\{\alpha\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial of degree <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq q</annotation></semantics></math>. Its "sum-of-powers" form is given by</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\alpha}(t)\;=\;\sum_{k=0}^{q}w^{(\alpha)}_{k}\,t^{k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>q</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\alpha}(t)\;=\;\sum_{k=0}^{q}w^{(\alpha)}_{k}\,t^{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the coefficients <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{(\alpha)}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{(\alpha)}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are uniquely determined by the Vandermonde system</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\alpha}\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;\alpha_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\alpha_{1}^{\,q-1}\\
1&amp;\alpha_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;\alpha_{2}^{\,q-1}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;\alpha_{q}&amp;\cdots&amp;\alpha_{q}^{\,q-1}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}w^{(\alpha)}_{0}\\
w^{(\alpha)}_{1}\\
\vdots\\
w^{(\alpha)}_{q-1}\end{bmatrix}\;=\;\begin{bmatrix}0\\
\cdots\\
1\\
\cdots\\
0\end{bmatrix}\!," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\alpha}\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;\alpha_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\alpha_{1}^{\,q-1}\\
1&amp;\alpha_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;\alpha_{2}^{\,q-1}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;\alpha_{q}&amp;\cdots&amp;\alpha_{q}^{\,q-1}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}w^{(\alpha)}_{0}\\
w^{(\alpha)}_{1}\\
\vdots\\
w^{(\alpha)}_{q-1}\end{bmatrix}\;=\;\begin{bmatrix}0\\
\cdots\\
1\\
\cdots\\
0\end{bmatrix}\!,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where the <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> on the RHS is in the row corresponding to <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Injecting (<a href="#A1.E21" title="In Appendix A Proofs ‣ CoVariance Filters and Neural Networks over Hilbert Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) in (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Definition 2 (Spatial Hilbert coVariance Filters). ‣ 3 Hilbert Covariance Filters and Neural Networks ‣ CoVariance Filters and Neural Networks over Hilbert Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), for any <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, it then holds</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{h}_{\alpha}(\hat{C}_{n})x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{h}_{\alpha}(\hat{C}_{n})x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{r}h_{\alpha}(\hat{\lambda}_{\ell})\,\left\langle x,\,\hat{\phi}_{\ell}\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,\hat{\phi}_{\ell}\;+\;h_{\alpha}(0)\,x_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell=1}^{r}h_{\alpha}(\hat{\lambda}_{\ell})\,\left\langle x,\,\hat{\phi}_{\ell}\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,\hat{\phi}_{\ell}\;+\;h_{\alpha}(0)\,x_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell\in I(\alpha)}\left\langle x,\,\hat{\phi}_{\ell}\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,\hat{\phi}_{\ell}=P_{\alpha}x." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\ell\in I(\alpha)}\left\langle x,\,\hat{\phi}_{\ell}\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,\hat{\phi}_{\ell}=P_{\alpha}x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Proposition 1.</span>
Fix <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{(m)}=S_{m}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{(m)}=S_{m}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{x}^{(m)}=S_{m}\bar{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{x}^{(m)}=S_{m}\bar{x}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle a,\,\hat{\mathbf{C}}_{n}^{(m)}b\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle a,\,\hat{\mathbf{C}}_{n}^{(m)}b\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{m}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\big\langle a,\;S_{m}(x_{i}-\bar{x})\big\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{m}}\big\langle S_{m}(x_{i}-\bar{x}),\;b\big\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\big\langle a,\;S_{m}(x_{i}-\bar{x})\big\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{m}}\big\langle S_{m}(x_{i}-\bar{x}),\;b\big\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{m}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(1)}{=}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left\langle x_{i}-\bar{x},\,S_{m}^{*}a\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\;\left\langle x_{i}-\bar{x},\,S_{m}^{*}b\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(1)}{=}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left\langle x_{i}-\bar{x},\,S_{m}^{*}a\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\;\left\langle x_{i}-\bar{x},\,S_{m}^{*}b\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(2)}{=}\left\langle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left\langle x_{i}-\bar{x},\,S_{m}^{*}b\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,(x_{i}-\bar{x})\;,\;S_{m}^{*}a\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(2)}{=}\left\langle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left\langle x_{i}-\bar{x},\,S_{m}^{*}b\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,(x_{i}-\bar{x})\;,\;S_{m}^{*}a\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(3)}{=}\left\langle S_{m}^{*}a,\,\hat{C}_{n}(S_{m}^{*}b)\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\overset{(4)}{=}\big\langle a,\;S_{m}\,\hat{C}_{n}\,S_{m}^{*}b\big\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{m}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">3</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(3)}{=}\left\langle S_{m}^{*}a,\,\hat{C}_{n}(S_{m}^{*}b)\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\overset{(4)}{=}\big\langle a,\;S_{m}\,\hat{C}_{n}\,S_{m}^{*}b\big\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{m}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where (1) uses the defining property of the adjoint, (2) uses linearity of the inner product, (3) applies the definition of <math id="A1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> applied to the vector <math id="A1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{*}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{*}b</annotation></semantics></math>, and (4) applies the adjoint identity again with <math id="A1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\hat{C}_{n}S_{m}^{*}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\hat{C}_{n}S_{m}^{*}b</annotation></semantics></math>. Since this holds for all <math id="A1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, the bilinear forms induced by <math id="A1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{C}}_{n}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{C}}_{n}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}\hat{C}_{n}S_{m}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}\hat{C}_{n}S_{m}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> agree.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Use-Cases for HVNs</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Ex. 1] Square-integrable Multivariate Real-valued Functions.</span>
Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=L^{2}(\mathbb{R},\beta;\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=L^{2}(\mathbb{R},\beta;\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> the Lebesgue measure. Let us denote with <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{B_{j}\}_{j=1}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B_{j}\}_{j=1}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> a collection of bins, i.e., a measurable partition with <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(B_{j})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(B_{j})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Set <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:=pd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:=pd</annotation></semantics></math> and fix any bijection <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota:\{1,\ldots,p\}\times\{1,\ldots,d\}\to\{1,\ldots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota:\{1,\ldots,p\}\times\{1,\ldots,d\}\to\{1,\ldots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math> to flatten <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,c)</annotation></semantics></math>-pairs into a single index.
Define <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}:\mathcal{H}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}:\mathcal{H}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> to perform channelwise bin-averaging by</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(S_{m}v)_{\iota(j,c)}\;=\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(S_{m}v)_{\iota(j,c)}\;=\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\sqrt{\beta(B_{j})}}\int_{B_{j}}v_{c}(t)\,d\beta(t),\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\sqrt{\beta(B_{j})}}\int_{B_{j}}v_{c}(t)\,d\beta(t),\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle j=1,\ldots,p,c=1,\ldots,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle j=1,\ldots,p,c=1,\ldots,d</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{*}a=\sum_{j=1}^{p}\sum_{c=1}^{d}a_{\iota(j,c)}\,s_{(j,c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{*}a=\sum_{j=1}^{p}\sum_{c=1}^{d}a_{\iota(j,c)}\,s_{(j,c)}</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{(j,c)}(t)\;=\;\beta(B_{j})^{-1/2}\,\mathbf{1}_{B_{j}}(t)\,e_{c}\;\in\;L^{2}(\mathbb{R},\beta;\mathbb{R}^{d})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">∈</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{(j,c)}(t)\;=\;\beta(B_{j})^{-1/2}\,\mathbf{1}_{B_{j}}(t)\,e_{c}\;\in\;L^{2}(\mathbb{R},\beta;\mathbb{R}^{d}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{c}\}_{c=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{c}\}_{c=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the canonical basis of <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Typical nonlinearities are pointwise Lipschitz transforms</p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma v)(t)\;=\;\sigma_{\ast}\!\big(v(t)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma v)(t)\;=\;\sigma_{\ast}\!\big(v(t)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ast}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ast}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> Lipschitz, e.g., componentwise ReLU.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark.</span> We constructively employed bin-averaging as a special intuitive case of a more general discretization approach. In particular, given any fixed orthonormal basis <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\psi_{j}\}_{j\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\psi_{j}\}_{j\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>–in the case of bin averaging, the orthonormal basis implicitly employed is the set of normalized bin indicators per channel, <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}:\mathcal{H}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}:\mathcal{H}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> can always be defined as "taking the first <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> coefficients in that basis", i.e.,</p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(S_{m}x)_{j}\;=\;\left\langle x,\,\psi_{j}\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}},\qquad j=1,\ldots,m," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{m}x)_{j}\;=\;\left\langle x,\,\psi_{j}\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}},\qquad j=1,\ldots,m,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{*}a\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{m}a_{j}\,\psi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{*}a\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{m}a_{j}\,\psi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words,
<math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{*}S_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{*}S_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal projector onto <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{span}\{\psi_{1},\ldots,\psi_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{span}\{\psi_{1},\ldots,\psi_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Ex. 2] Square-summable Real-valued Sequences</span>
Let <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\ell^{2}(\mathbb{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\ell^{2}(\mathbb{N})</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}:\ell^{2}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}:\ell^{2}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> can be defined as the canonical projection as</p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(S_{m}v)_{j}\;=\;v_{j},\qquad j=1,\dots,m," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{m}v)_{j}\;=\;v_{j},\qquad j=1,\dots,m,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{*}a=\sum_{j=1}^{m}a_{j}e_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{*}a=\sum_{j=1}^{m}a_{j}e_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{*}S_{m}=P_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{*}S_{m}=P_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is again the orthogonal projector onto the first <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> coordinates. Typical nonlinearities are pointwise Lipschitz maps</p>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma v)_{k}\;=\;\sigma_{\ast}(v_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma v)_{k}\;=\;\sigma_{\ast}(v_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Ex. 3] Reproducing Kernel Hilbert Spaces.</span>
Let <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\mathcal{H}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\mathcal{H}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be the reproducing kernel Hilbert space on a set <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> with kernel <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:\mathcal{T}\times\mathcal{T}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:\mathcal{T}\times\mathcal{T}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For sampling locations <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{j}\}_{j=1}^{m}\subset\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{j}\}_{j=1}^{m}\subset\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, point evaluation is bounded and the representers are <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(\cdot,t_{j})\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(\cdot,t_{j})\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}:\mathcal{H}_{K}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}:\mathcal{H}_{K}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> can be defined as</p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(S_{m}v)_{j}\;=\;v(t_{j})\;=\;\left\langle v,\,K(\cdot,t_{j})\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}},\qquad j=1,\dots,m," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{m}v)_{j}\;=\;v(t_{j})\;=\;\left\langle v,\,K(\cdot,t_{j})\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}},\qquad j=1,\dots,m,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">so the adjoint is <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{m}^{*}a\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{m}a_{j}\,K(\cdot,t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{m}^{*}a\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{m}a_{j}\,K(\cdot,t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. A convenient class of admissible nonlinearities is given by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite></p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(v)\;=\;S_{m}^{*}\,\sigma_{\ast}(S_{m}v)\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{m}\sigma_{\ast}\!\big((S_{m}v)_{j}\big)\,K(\cdot,t_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(v)\;=\;S_{m}^{*}\,\sigma_{\ast}(S_{m}v)\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{m}\sigma_{\ast}\!\big((S_{m}v)_{j}\big)\,K(\cdot,t_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ast}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ast}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> Lipschitz.</p>
</div>
